.TH PERSO_FREEBSD 9 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Kernel Developer's Manual"
.SH NAME
perso_freebsd \- FreeBSD i386 binary compatibility personality
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/exec/perso/personality.h>
.PP
.BI "extern struct personality " personality_freebsd ";"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B perso_freebsd
personality allows the kernel to execute FreeBSD i386 binaries. It implements the FreeBSD system call table and handles OS-specific behaviors.
.SH SYSTEM CALLS
The system call table follows the FreeBSD ABI:
.TP
.B SYS_exit (1)
Terminate process.
.TP
.B SYS_fork (2)
Create process.
.TP
.B SYS_read (3)
Read input.
.TP
.B SYS_write (4)
Write output.
.TP
.B SYS_uname (164)
Note that this differs significantly from Linux/Native (usually 122). This implementation returns a `struct freebsd_utsname` identifying the system as "FreeBSD 14.3-RELEASE-p5".
.SH LIMITATIONS
.IP * 2
Global/Static syscall table implementation.
.IP * 2
Missing deep structure conversion for `stat`, `dirent`, etc. (Direct mapping is used where ABIs coincidentally overlap).
.IP * 2
Tracing metadata (`syscall_names`, `syscall_fmts`) is currently unimplemented for this personality, meaning syscall traces will show raw numbers and hex arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR personality (9),
.BR perso_native (9),
.BR perso_linux (9)
